ergy and a sufficiently small saxion slope without balancing several unrelated contributions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e95c5104ebe75500827ba7d5b7559c993b431335aca56550b91916df0d720bc0","title":"Can a gauge interaction provide enough damping for a sub-Planckian-decay-constant axion to inflate on its naturally steep cosine potential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0054"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e921d7aeaac23e7fa0d42ca275418513603a298ecbea027f146afefa8054d426","title":"Can cosmological survival after the QCD transition jointly select a small nonzero Higgs vev and a small strong-CP angle, without Peccei–Quinn relaxation, and produce correlated dark-matter and EDM signals?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e963c7df7428e3eef33cc96712a6a1ce8831cab60ae564b68557b0b9ea5e323a","title":"Can sphere free energy, or its Legendre transform, yield monotonic F-functions in a top-down holographic model beyond minimally coupled Einstein-scalar gravity, including a curvature-driven phase transition?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e9855f47ea25af8971436c56841b89b0678c8bad0e7f4d331b7cd56ea225112f","title":"Can interrupted monodromy inflation remain compatible with the paper-era CMB bounds when strong-coupling kinetic corrections are included, and what correlated non-Gaussianity and shorter-wavelength gravitational-wave signatures result?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e938130dc5f7e49e501bbf1b305e66b4b84b4b65660c7551c20724d533c64d5a","title":"Can a dedicated spatial-template analysis of Galactic Hawking-emission photons in